## Hints

- E1: df = (a+b)²/(a²/(n₁−1) + b²/(n₂−1)) with a = s₁²/n₁, b = s₂²/n₂.
  It lives near the LARGER sample when variances are similar.
- E2: the dividend formula only needs ρ and the SD ratio; you can
  reproduce the observed ratio to ~2 significant figures.
- E3: ×252 multiplies the mean, the SE, and the CI — the t-stat is
  unchanged by annualization. The caveat: volatility clustering makes
  the daily observations non-iid.
